::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.330
Nico Robin is steadily
approaching the Gates of Justice...

3
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.780
while we're here fighting like this.

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.990
Or maybe I should say that from
her perspective, she's approaching hell?

5
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.230
Yeah, I know.

6
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.370
It's true.

7
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.970
Robin-chan's life is at stake!

8
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.220
But if you get in my way,

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.750
I won't go easy on you
just because you're a woman!

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.720
Hand over that key
before you get hurt!

11
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.180
Raising your voice won't yield the key.

12
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.890
You don't have to treat me like a woman.

13
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.310
I don't live in such a delicate world.

14
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.570
Since we've got an extermination order,

15
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.820
I'll just take your life,
that's all.

16
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.960
You can't have it.

17
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.300
I just want...

18
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.170
the key to Robin-chan's handcuffs.

19
00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.460
Then I guess teatime is over?

20
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.680
Shave!

21
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.140
Your power is indeed
that of a superhuman.

22
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:27.520
An opening!

23
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.030
I landed a blow.

24
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.580
Hey! How could you?!

25
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.290
Isn't that what you call
“landing a blow”?

26
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.010
How dare you...? You little...

27
00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.130
Moon Walk!

28
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.700
He's fast!

29
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.750
I've just stomped you.

30
00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.110
That means you lost!

31
00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.650
Now, give me the key...

32
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.590
Finger Pistol!

33
00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.800
Tempest Kick!

34
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.470
What a disappointing man.

35
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.270
You're a pirate,

36
00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.300
and yet, you're quite the coward!

37
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.310
Hey, shut up!

38
00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.900
Give me the key!

39
00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.650
I've had enough of your
transparent threats.

40
00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.330
Shall we try something fun?

41
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.640
You're dead unless you fight back.

42
00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.650
<b>Mr. Chivalry</b>

43
00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.910
He's not coming after me.

44
00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.750
<b>First Floor - Receiving Area
Nami vs. Kumadori</b>

45
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.000
Good!

46
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.130
If I'd have been caught again,
I'd be dead.

47
00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.210
I'll just run and...

48
00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.920
Life Return!

49
00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.510
Oh, shoot!

50
00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:36.230
Now, shall I...

51
00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.300
pierce you to death...

52
00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.690
or choke you to death?!

53
00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.770
A wintry blast blows through this world.

54
00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:52.490
Your peaceful rest comes before the first buds of spring.

55
00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.150
At least once more,

56
00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:03.560
you shall bloom lovely scarlet petals...

57
00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.440
before you fall!

58
00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.370
My duty is to offer such compassion!

59
00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:20.020
When you arrive in the afterlife,

60
00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:24.020
please tell my late mother...

61
00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.360
that I'm... I'm doing fine...

62
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.490
as an assassin!

63
00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.200
Now, die!

64
00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.050
Now... Now... Now!

65
00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:38.870
No!

66
00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:43.300
Song of Spring Spirit!

67
00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.470
Cloven Roseo!

68
00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.940
Nami! Are you okay?!

69
00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.160
Chopper,

70
00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.070
Thanks. You saved me.

71
00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.860
What's with that guy?

72
00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.140
Does he have a devil fruit power?

73
00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.470
I don't know.

74
00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:16.330
His hair moves like an octopus,
so I couldn't do anything.

75
00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.570
More importantly,
now is our chance, Chopper.

76
00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.170
Let's get out of here right away.

77
00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.590
Why?!

78
00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.650
Unless we defeat him,
we can't get the key.

79
00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:25.880
You mean this, right?

80
00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.580
I stole the key without him noticing,
but I just couldn't get away from him.

81
00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.380
Do you know what's going on
with the others?

82
00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:36.330
Say, Nami.

83
00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.810
What number does it have on it?

84
00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.500
Number?

85
00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.750
It says 3.

86
00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.730
Wrong one.

87
00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.520
What is this number?

88
00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.740
Something fell down!

89
00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.780
Is it... a doll?!

90
00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.200
No.

91
00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:57.910
Sanji!

92
00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.400
Why does he look like this?!

93
00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.420
Sanji!

94
00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.890
Hey! What happened?!

95
00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.000
Why is your body like this?!

96
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.710
Are you okay, Sanji-kun?!

97
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.380
Sanji!

98
00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.130
Sorry, I lost.

99
00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.840
I couldn't get the key.

100
00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:27.780
Hold on a sec, Sanji.
I'll give you first aid.

101
00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:31.320
I never thought that Sanji-kun
would lose.

102
00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.830
Sanji-kun,

103
00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.540
Were you really
not able to defeat her?

104
00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.040
Did you give her an honest fight?

105
00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:51.080
It was that woman who
you fought, wasn't it?

106
00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.550
You're soft with women.

107
00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:57.320
I'm sorry about the key.

108
00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.530
That's not it!

109
00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.560
I'm saying that because
of that stupid chivalry,

110
00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.230
you could die!

111
00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.160
You're gonna stick to it even
after getting hurt like this?!

112
00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.940
What would we do without you?!

113
00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.740
It's not like...

114
00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.940
I want to die.

115
00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.390
It's just that,

116
00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:18.130
I was raised with the idea that kicking women is wrong beaten into me.

117
00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.780
So,

118
00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.690
even at the cost of my life,

119
00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:25.240
I won't kick a woman!

120
00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.630
You're an idiot.

121
00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.590
Stupid!

122
00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.540
Hey! What're you doing, Nami?!

123
00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.240
If running away also violates your code of chivalry,

124
00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.640
at least ditch that part of it!

125
00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.080
It's not worth dying in vain.

126
00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.890
Leave that woman to me.

127
00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.170
Also,

128
00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.900
I think a little more of your
code of chivalry than I did before.

129
00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:54.810
What?!

130
00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:57.000
Did she just say
that she loves me more?

131
00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.570
No, she didn't!

132
00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.830
I'm not kind.

133
00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.570
Neither am I.

134
00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.040
Sounds like we can get along.

135
00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:30.260
Hold it!

136
00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.270
The octopus guy!

137
00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.720
I won't...

138
00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:38.540
I won't let you get away!

139
00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.960
Nami, you go deal with that woman!

140
00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.700
I'll do something about this guy!

141
00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.050
Okay!

142
00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.340
Are you getting in my way?!

143
00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:50.440
Cloven...

144
00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.400
Cross!

145
00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.310
Whoa! Pirate guy!

146
00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.110
What're you doing?!

147
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:22.120
Seriously, there's no way you can cross
water like this on a boat, now is there?

148
00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.620
Are you an idiot?!

149
00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:28.670
But Robin was taken to those gates!

150
00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:33.330
Unless I hurry up, I won't
be able to bring her back!

151
00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.670
Wait, pirate guy!

152
00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.170
Calm down!

153
00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:44.160
We came to tell you how to
get to the Gates of Justice!

154
00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:44.850
What?

155
00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.180
Anyhow, you're amazing.

156
00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.180
I'm impressed that you knew
about a passage like this!

157
00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:57.320
I saw Lucci's lackey going down
the stairs, laughing very loudly.

158
00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.450
So I followed them.

159
00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:06.660
Box reads “The Lackey”

160
00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.300
If they don't know where the entrance is,
they can't come after us!

161
00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:06.660
Serves them right!

162
00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.620
Lucci and that black-haired lady
went through the doors, too.

163
00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.390
So these are them, huh?

164
00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.450
They're really heavy-duty iron doors.

165
00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.000
Do you know how to open them?

166
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.090
The lackey was doing something over here,

167
00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.190
so I bet you can control
them with this keyhole!

168
00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.820
We don't have the key, though.

169
00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.960
You guys, step back.

170
00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.180
Huh? What're you gonna do?

171
00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.340
We can go to the Gates of
Justice through here, right?

172
00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.760
Er... Yeah.

173
00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.470
Gear Third!

174
00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.540
They opened!

175
00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.250
All right! I'm heading there now!

176
00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.720
What?! How come you're small now?!

177
00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.360
That pirate guy sure is interesting!

178
00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.500
I-I just heard a loud noise.

179
00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.570
Was that my imagination?

180
00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.280
No, it couldn't have been.

181
00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:13.340
Could that noise have been one of
the pirates destroying the doors?

182
00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:15.750
What?! Such a ridiculous idea isn't possible!

183
00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.350
Those are thick iron doors!

184
00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:22.170
Besides, there's no way that
they could find those doors!

185
00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:27.300
Well, they should know where they are,
since a child and her pet were following us.

186
00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.520
What?!

187
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.740
I-If you knew that,
why didn't you kill them?!

188
00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.560
Because...

189
00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.810
I received no such order.

190
00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.980
What?! You dimwit!

191
00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.900
For something so trivial,
use your own discretion!

192
00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.730
Couldn't you imagine what'd happen if
you didn't do anything about it?!

193
00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.320
So what're you saying?!

194
00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.450
Are you saying that
someone's headed this way?!

195
00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.500
All right! Back to normal!

196
00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.460
Just wait, Robin!

197
00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:10.180
I'll be sure to beat the crap
out of that pigeon guy!

198
00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:16.600
<b>Pantry Front Passage
Franky vs. Fukuro</b>

199
00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:15.860
Dammit! I need to refill
my cola as soon as possible.

200
00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:21.440
For someone with such a large body,
he sure does like to bounce around.

201
00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:27.570
I'm right here.

202
00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:34.080
Seems like you're at least quick
when it comes to escaping.

203
00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.790
I'm under no obligation to take
the punches you're so proud of.

204
00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.460
Franky Triangle Jacker!

205
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.340
No way...

206
00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.720
I'd get hit by sideburns like that!

207
00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:52.540
I've got you!

208
00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.810
Weapons Left!

209
00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.260
Seems like I'm almost out of cola.

210
00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.990
I'd better get to the kitchen now!

211
00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.320
Hold it!

212
00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.320
Dammit! He dodged my attack!

213
00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.530
Damn wimp, you're an
expert at running away!

214
00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:16.410
What'd you say?!

215
00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.950
What's the matter, wimp?

216
00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.830
You're not running away this time?

217
00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.400
You bastard!

218
00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.300
You made me mad with what you said!

219
00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.840
Take my killer fist!

220
00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:35.180
It's a super heavy punch combined
with Finger Pistol's speed!

221
00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.330
Tough Dugong!

222
00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:46.550
What a puny, ineffective punch!

223
00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:49.190
Strong...

224
00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.630
Iron Body!

225
00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.270
Hammer!

226
00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:00.990
That was a pathetic punch.

227
00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.660
Tough Dugong!

228
00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:21.550
Your punches are flabby.

229
00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:23.880
No.

230
00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.990
Your punches are limp.

231
00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:29.690
Then, your punches are flimsy.

232
00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:33.030
Your underpants are lazy.

233
00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.070
Underpants?

234
00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.900
They're not punches!

235
00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.940
Underpants! That's what you are!

236
00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.900
You damn bra!

237
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.860
Shut up, socks!

238
00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:44.730
Long johns!

239
00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:45.620
Loose shorts!

240
00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.670
Loincloth!

241
00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.880
Get off of me, you bastard!

242
00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.550
Shut up, coin purse!

243
00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.270
Great!

244
00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:04.160
I made it into the kitchen!

245
00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.620
There it is! A huge refrigerator!

246
00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.370
Is that him?

247
00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:17.490
He probably has a gorilla-type devil fruit power.

248
00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.270
Dammit!

249
00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:21.470
Three minutes have already passed?

250
00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:25.270
I used the rumble ball too soon.

251
00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.290
What am I gonna do?

252
00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.880
Depart the three planes of existence!

253
00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.760
Your life ends here!

254
00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.000
You bastard!

255
00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.010
Good! It's got a lock!

256
00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.560
Kumadori!

257
00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:51.600
All right! I locked him in!

258
00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.920
How dare you?!

259
00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.600
Hey, hold on a sec, gorilla!

260
00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.990
I need that fridge!

261
00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.570
Ahh! CP9 and the punk!

262
00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.840
I'm Franky! I'm on your side, remember?!

263
00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:02.990
Who'd you call a gorilla?!

264
00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:03.740
You're too slow!

265
00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.480
Listen.

266
00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:09.070
Just like Luffy,
I haven't forgiven you yet.

267
00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:11.320
The reason Usopp left us was...

268
00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.430
It's all your fault!

269
00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:17.090
Give us Usopp back!

270
00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:20.130
Like I said, you guys
were with him earlier.

271
00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.640
That's not important right now!

272
00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.640
Don't you wanna save Nico Robin?!

273
00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.600
I do! Robin!

274
00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.680
Then get three bottles of cola from
that fridge and give them to me!

275
00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.970
With cola, I can power up!

276
00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:38.280
I'll take care of these guys in
an instant and take their keys!

277
00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.690
What kind of idiot actually
gets stronger with cola?

278
00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.450
Shut up! That'd be me!

279
00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:46.180
Just how long...

280
00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:49.530
are you planning to
keep up the comedy act?!

281
00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:52.890
On top of that, you're trying to
have a tea break during a fight?

282
00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:54.800
How rude!

283
00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.190
Tough Dugong Esoterica:

284
00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.760
Owl Thrashing!

285
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.940
Beans Left!

286
00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.760
What was that?!

287
00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.450
Ahh! This is terrible!

288
00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.700
That's right!
He's on our side right now!

289
00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.660
I'll do what he told me to.

290
00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.810
If I open the door and close it in less than a second, he can't come out!

291
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:42.170
The door has...

292
00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.630
All right!

293
00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.920
Franky!

294
00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.720
You're a lifesaver!

295
00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:58.770
Fresh!

296
00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.240
What the...?

297
00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:08.030
Freshness is most important!
Vegetable Punch! Take this!

298
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.160
Tough Dugong.

299
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.330
Hey! That was vegetable juice!

300
00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:17.830
Who's prioritizing health around here, you bastard?!

301
00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.920
Give me cola!

302
00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.800
Oh, so it wasn't because he was thirsty.

303
00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.760
The door...

304
00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:26.790
Here you go!

305
00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.010
Thanks!

306
00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:34.980
I'm feeling good!

307
00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.940
Well,

308
00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.690
let me take a rest.

309
00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.980
My work in
the field is done for now.

310
00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.580
Stop being so upset.

311
00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.360
Don't fight.

312
00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:48.490
Why don't you have some tea?

313
00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.990
Tea wouldn't...

314
00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:53.450
give me energy! You moron!

315
00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:56.750
He's... funny.

316
00:21:56.980 --> 00:21:57.840
Hey!

317
00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:02.390
What's with that “I wonder what
happens with other drinks” look?!

318
00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.450
This'll be the last time, you damn deer!

319
00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.550
So it doesn't depend
on how you're feeling?

320
00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:08.720
I need only cola!

321
00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:13.810
That's it! Without a doubt!

322
00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.430
Thanks!

323
00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:22.230
I don't know what the deal is,
but I'm not gonna let you have your way!

324
00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.270
Tempest Kick!

325
00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:26.240
Franky!

326
00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:40.550
Super!

327
00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.360
What's the deal?

328
00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:09.990
It's not like drinking cola would
make a difference or anything.

329
00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:14.530
Put up your guard.

330
00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:16.890
What a fool.

331
00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.910
Are you gonna give me
another pathetic punch?

332
00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:23.670
Strong... Hammer!

333
00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:44.690
Whoooa! Amazing!

334
00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:05.720
Sorry.

335
00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:09.070
My punches earlier were...

336
00:24:09.070 --> 00:24:11.550
indeed pathetic.
